      "writtenOn": "2026-07-24T13:23:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is by far not enough. There are many more special characters in a regex than just `.` and `*`. To mention some of them: `+`, `?`, `(`, `)`, `[`, `]`, `{`, `}`, ...\n\nSee here [1] for a complete java regex syntax.\n\nThe `Pattern` class already provides the feature you need here, the `Pattern.quote(...)` method [2].\nTake the prefix which is everything but the last `*`, apply `Pattern.quote(prefix)` and append `.*` at the end:\n```\n  String prefix \u003d pattern.substring(0, pattern.length() - 1);\n  String regex \u003d \"^\" + Pattern.quote(prefix) + \".*\";\n```\n\n[1] https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/util/regex/Pattern.html\n[2] https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/util/regex/Pattern.html#quote(java.lang.String)",
